WHAT COULD NOT BE ESTABLISHED, stated plainly
---------------------------------------------

The licence above was read from version **0.145.0** of the npm distribution. It was
NOT read from either of the two builds this crate's material was actually extracted
from, and that gap is real rather than pedantic:

  * The standalone release directories for 0.147.0 and 0.153.4 ship **no `LICENSE`
    and no `NOTICE` file at all** (verified by listing the whole of each release
    tree: each contains `bin/`, `codex-package.json`, `codex-path/`,
    `codex-resources/`, a `codex -> bin/codex` symlink, and nothing else), and
    `codex-package.json` carries only `layoutVersion`,
    `version`, `target`, `variant`, `entrypoint`, `resourcesDir` and `pathDir` — no
    licence field.
  * The vendored JSON and the completion-derived argv census carry no headers of any
    kind; they are machine output.
  * No file anywhere in this repository states an upstream licence, and
    `schema-0.147/PROVENANCE.md` — otherwise the most detailed record of where this
    material came from — does not mention licensing at all.

So the chain is: the 0.147.0/0.153.4 binaries identify themselves as
`github.com/openai/codex` and as the `@openai/codex` npm package; that npm package,
at the one version available here, declares Apache-2.0. That is a sound inference
about the project and it is an inference across versions about the artifacts. If the
exact licence of a specific release matters — for a redistribution question, say —
re-check it against the `LICENSE` file in `github.com/openai/codex` at the tag for
that release rather than trusting this note.


What is and is not derived from upstream
----------------------------------------

**No upstream source code is vendored here.** What is vendored is upstream's own
machine-generated self-description, further processed by CodeConnect's code:

  * `schema-{0.147,0.153}/guarded-wire-{stable,experimental}.json` — a *projection*,
    computed by `codex_broker::guarded_surface`, of the JSON Schema bundle emitted by
    `codex app-server generate-json-schema`. Only the methods the broker guards are
    kept; the rest of the schema is discarded.
  * `schema-{0.147,0.153}/guarded-argv.json` — the root subcommand and flag tokens
    parsed out of the `opts="…"` line of `codex completion bash`.
  * `schema-0.147/methods-{stable,experimental}.json` — the list of method *names* in
    those same bundles.

Everything else in the crate — `schema-0.147/disposition-matrix.tsv`, both
`PROVENANCE.md` files, this NOTICE, and all of `src/` — is CodeConnect's own work
under the repository's MIT licence.

Full regeneration recipes, and the reasoning about why these files exist and are
never re-derived from the binary being checked, are in
`schema-0.147/PROVENANCE.md` and `schema-0.153/PROVENANCE.md`.
